{"availability":"unavailable","full":"aavainav/atom.forms","name":"atom.forms","description":"A layered, immutable form engine for building complex domain forms (traffic citations, crash reports, etc.) with validation, printing, and reporting.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-08T16:01:25Z","updated":"2026-10-06T20:17:58Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["bootstrap","react","react-router","typescript","zod"],"demo":"https://atom-forms.netlify.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:56:56.321Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T07:56:56.321Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T22:54:21.718Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T22:54:21.718Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-09T05:47:19.220Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-12T07:56:56.321Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A form engine for law-enforcement paper forms, and the forms themselves.","A citation or a collision report is a printed document with a fixed layout, a defined set of boxes, and rules about what may go in them. This repository models that directly: a definition tree describes the shape of a form, an entity tree holds its values, and a form package renders the result to look like the paper it stands in for — so what an officer fills in on screen is recognisably the form they would otherwise fill in by hand.","Six forms across three states are implemented today, along with the engine, the registries they draw on, and a sandbox app to run them in."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aavainav/atom.forms/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a52f9e170046aed595b21677f1e624ad6c2a16687edfe7efd39b10813a23f299","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T22:54:21.828Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T22:54:21.828Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A form engine for law-enforcement paper forms, and the forms themselves.","sour